atlas model
# The model estate is not one architecture. FPQ alone is at least three: the
# weight transformation, the seed-program calculus it searches, and the per-block
# mode selection. Each has its own node ontology and its own maturity. None of
# them may claim the others' evidence.

architecture fpq-transform
  owns FPQRepresentation
  consumes ResourcePressure
  publishes FPQRepresentation
  canonical_name FPQTransformationGraph
  family model
  domain Model Representation
  layer model/representation
  semantic_question Can these weights be reconstructed within tolerance from a compact functional representation?
  purpose Store seed programs, not weights. Functional Polar Quantization of a weight tensor.
  maturity measured
  node_types WeightTensor
  node_types PolarDecomposition
  node_types ResidualField
  node_types FPQRepresentation
  edge_types decomposes_into
  edge_types leaves_residual
  edge_types reconstructs_to
  internal_calculus RandomSigns/FWHT
  internal_calculus RecursiveS^N-PolarDecomposition
  internal_calculus ExpectedAngularStructure
  internal_calculus SeedDiscovery
  internal_calculus QJLResidual
  invariant reconstruction is deterministic byte-for-byte across runs on the same fixture
  forbidden_inference low reconstruction error -> good semantic generation quality
  forbidden_inference reconstruction within tolerance -> SLI execution correctness
  forbidden_inference fixture reconstruction -> qwen model reconstruction
  computational_form fused
  native_format axon
  native_format crux
  command BonfyreFPQ
  invariant a distortion diagnostic is accumulated once; two passes summing into one accumulator that is divided once inflated the reported pre-RVQ RMSE by the square root of two and nothing downstream could have noticed
  invariant a diagnostic reconstructs in the encoder's own lattice scale; a local named lattice_scale shadowing it with wnorm/padded put scaled_orig three orders of magnitude below the lattice points it was differenced against, and the post RMSE became minus the lattice point
  invariant disabling the correction must make the post error identically the residual, because every tile is then the zeroed tile; that identity is the test, and it cannot be satisfied by a metric measured in the wrong space
  invariant a percentage is called a reduction only when the error fell; a -6241% reduction is a sentence with no meaning and it sat beside a genuine 0.9998 cosine without stopping anything
  forbidden_inference a high cosine -> coherent diagnostics
  forbidden_inference a printed reduction -> an improvement
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/tests/rvq_metric_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/src/fpq_native.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/src/ggml_reader.c
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/fpq_evidence.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/fpq_pack_evidence.py.archive
  witness packs/fpq-proof-frontier/fixtures/tiny-f16.gguf
  witness packs/fpq-proof-frontier/measured-witness.yaff
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/results/2026-09-11-qwen-fpq0-header.json
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/results/2026-09-11-qwen2.5-coder-0.5b-real-tensor-v9.json measures a real 114,688-weight Qwen2.5-Coder-0.5B attention tensor through FPQ v9 transform/reconstruction (v9 cosine 0.999935 at 5.75 bits/weight, 1.23 seconds on the recorded host); the receipt explicitly excludes layer, logit, generation and task claims
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/results/2026-09-24-qwen2.5-coder-3b-attnq-v9.json measures a 4,194,304-weight Qwen2.5-Coder-3B Q4_K_M attention matrix through v8 and v9: v9 cosine 0.999939 at 4.32 bits/weight versus v8 0.999860 at 4.16 bits/weight; the receipt explicitly records the quality/size trade-off and excludes whole-model or runtime claims
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/results/2026-09-11-bitnetcpp-arm-build-refusal.json records the unmodified upstream Microsoft BitNet.cpp ARM build refusal before model execution, so the official model artifact is not mistaken for a local BitNet runtime witness
  witness cmd/BonfyreQwenFPQ/results/2026-09-11-qwen-native-fp16-execution.json records the existing 290-tensor Qwen FPQ0 artifact through the native 24-layer runtime and four generated tokens; it is an all-passthrough native-fp16 baseline, not FPQ block execution or FPQ parity
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_fpq_evidence.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/fpq_pack_evidence.py.archive
  witness ~/BonfyreModels/fpq/*.fpq-pack.json (recorded substrate quality gates)
  source_lineage run4_institutional_fabric FPQ archive
  source_lineage mature fpqqwen substrate (HuggingFace, cmd/BonfyreQwenFPQ, ~/BonfyreModels/fpq)
  known_gap a real Qwen2.5-Coder-0.5B FPQ0 artifact is structurally header-verified (290 tensors / 494032768 weights) and now traverses native layer execution/generation as all passthrough tensors. The full non-passthrough FPQ population, block-local consumption, layer/logit/generation parity and useful runtime envelope remain uncompleted; the current quantitative whole-model fixture remains synthetic-but-structured
  known_gap recorded fpqqwen packs show semantic_behavior OPEN (generation parity failed) -- honest, not laundered
  reheat_condition reconstruction fixture mse exceeds ceiling
  reheat_condition fixture gguf hash changes

architecture fpq-seed
  canonical_name FPQSeedProgramGraph
  family model
  domain Model Representation
  layer model/representation
  semantic_question What combinator program reproduces this weight block's angular structure?
  purpose The combinator calculus FPQ searches: ROT PAIR SCALE SHIFT REP FOLD LERP FREQ RAMP REFINE DBREF CHURCH DCT.
  maturity implemented
  node_types SeedProgram
  node_types Combinator
  edge_types recursive_dependency
  edge_types refinement_branch
  internal_calculus combinator-depth-and-parameter-search
  forbidden_inference seed found for a block -> seed generalizes to the tensor
  computational_form fused
  native_format helix
  command BonfyreFPQ
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/src/seed.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/src/seed_v1.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/src/serialize.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/tests/serialization.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/tests/serialization_faults.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/serialization.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/tests/serialization_contract.cue
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/tests/serialization.c verifies exact dictionary byte factoring, decoded parity with base seeds and both seed modes, independent block distortion and QJL words, legacy v1-v3 and interim v4 compatibility, truncation refusal, bounded malformed parsing and preservation of an existing destination after a failed save
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/tests/serialization_faults.c injects failure at every observed serializer allocation in legacy loading, dictionary saving and nested dictionary cloning; failed loads return no tensors and failed saves preserve the existing file
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/Makefile test-serialization validates C-emitted metadata from the actual dictionary file, empty tensor and four legacy headers against serialization.cue, and checks twelve malformed metadata refusals covering version, flags, layout, counts, mode, dictionary references and QJL word lengths
  invariant the owner-local CUE contract constrains projected header and block-dictionary relations; the native parser and tests own binary framing, exact tree bytes, resource bounds and decoded parity
  invariant FPQ! version 4 flag 1 selects the exact seed dictionary; version 4 flag 0 retains the interim per-block layout and no parser guesses between them
  invariant dictionary identity includes target dimension and exact combinator bytes, including signed zero, while each block retains its own distortion, radius and QJL payload
  invariant failed saves leave the previous destination intact; malformed or partial loads return no tensors, and unsupported coordinate or auxiliary payloads refuse instead of being discarded
  forbidden_inference fewer stored seed bytes or unchanged decoded fixture values -> whole-model quality, useful inference or a model compression ratio
  known_gap dictionary sharing factors the FPQ! file only; loading clones each block program for existing ownership and cleanup, and FPQ0 coordinate serialization remains a separate owner
  known_gap structural correctness only partially witnessed
  source_lineage run4_institutional_fabric FPQ archive

architecture fpq-mode-select
  canonical_name FPQModeSelectionGraph
  family model
  domain Model Representation
  layer model/representation
  semantic_question Which decomposition mode (FWHT / DIRECT / COORD) minimizes error-plus-cost for this block?
  purpose Lazy/thunk-based per-block mode selection; distinct from the seed combinator graph.
  maturity implemented
  # Demoted: every witness this carried was archived. The evidence was
  # retired and the claim was never revisited, which is the laundering the
  # atlas forbids -- reclaiming measured needs a witness that runs today.
  known_gap fpq-mode-select lost its live witness to archival and holds implemented until one runs again
  node_types FPQBlock
  node_types ModeCandidate
  edge_types scored_by
  edge_types selects
  internal_calculus thunk-eval FWHT|DIRECT|COORD@k
  forbidden_inference chosen mode on one block -> best mode on another
  computational_form fused
  command BonfyreFPQ
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFPQ/src/fpq_codec_v2.c
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_fpq_evidence.py.archive
  source_lineage run4_institutional_fabric FPQ archive

