architecture vector-body-admission
  canonical_name VectorBodyAdmission
  family learning
  domain Learning
  maturity measured
  semantic_question Does the store hold the body it was offered, and does it say so when it does not?
  # The vector insert discarded the result of its own step. A body of the wrong
  # width is rejected by the vector table, but the metadata row had already been
  # written and the counter had already been incremented, so a run reporting
  # `inserted: 1` left `artifacts: 1, vectors: 0` and exited zero. The store
  # held an artifact with no body and nothing said so.
  #
  # Underneath it the parser stopped at the store's width, so a longer vector was
  # truncated and stored as though whole -- worse than a refusal, because the
  # store then holds a different vector from the one offered and every neighbour
  # computed against it is wrong in a way nothing records.
  node_types VectorBody
  node_types ArtifactRow
  edge_types stored_as
  state_types stored
  state_types refused
  invariant a body whose width differs from the store's is refused before anything is written, so a refusal leaves nothing behind
  invariant the result of every write is checked, and only a write that completed increments the count
  invariant an import offered input and storing nothing exits non-zero; exiting zero after storing nothing is how an empty store comes to be believed populated
  invariant a parser reports the real length it was offered rather than the length it could accept; truncating to the accepted width stores a different vector under the offered one's name
  invariant the artifact count and the vector count are two halves of one record and never disagree
  forbidden_inference a reported insert -> a stored body
  forbidden_inference a stored vector -> a correct or current one
  computational_form storage
  native_format json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreVec/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreVec/tests/width_admission_test.sh
  measured a 32-wide and a 512-wide body are both refused with the real width named, leaving zero artifacts and zero vectors; a 384-wide body stores one of each
  witness 2026-10-12 cmd/BonfyreVec/tests/width_admission_test.sh (24 checks) creates a store with init --dims 768, stores and finds a 768-wide body, refuses a 384-wide one without leaving a row, and refuses to re-make an existing store at another width; insert now reads the width from the store's own declaration instead of a compiled constant
  known_gap a store is still one width for its whole life; changing embedding model means making a new store and re-embedding, and nothing migrates one
